<zk xmlns:n="native" xmlns:ca="client/attribute">
	<n:p>
	Codeeditor (ZK CE, since 11.0.0) is a syntax-highlighting source editor: line
	numbers, edit history, nine grammars and a light/dark surface, wrapping a
	CodeMirror 6 editor. Use it wherever a page edits or shows code - an XML or
	JSON config, a SQL statement, an HTML template - instead of a plain textbox.
	It reports edits through the same onChanging/onChange InputEvent as the other
	input components, so value binds exactly like a textbox value does.
	</n:p>
	<n:p>
	Two things to know before the first example. It takes no children, so a
	multi-line initial value goes in through &lt;attribute name="value"&gt; -
	an XML attribute would collapse the newlines to spaces. And it has no
	intrinsic height: give it one, or it grows with the content instead of
	scrolling.
	</n:p>

	<n:h1>Basic</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	language picks the grammar, height fixes the box; the editor scrolls inside it
	</n:p>
	<codeeditor language="java" height="160px" width="600px">
		<attribute name="value">public class Greeter {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		System.out.println("Hello, ZK 11");
	}
}</attribute>
	</codeeditor>

	<n:h1>Languages</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	nine grammars ship in the CE build: plain, html, xml, java, javascript, css,
	json, sql and markdown. plain is the default and means no highlighting;
	an unrecognised value raises a WrongValueException. Switching language at
	runtime re-highlights the same document in place.
	</n:p>
	<hlayout valign="middle">
		<label value="language"/>
		<combobox id="langPicker" readonly="true" value="javascript" width="140px"
				  onChange="sampler.setLanguage(self.getValue())">
			<comboitem label="plain"/>
			<comboitem label="html"/>
			<comboitem label="xml"/>
			<comboitem label="java"/>
			<comboitem label="javascript"/>
			<comboitem label="css"/>
			<comboitem label="json"/>
			<comboitem label="sql"/>
			<comboitem label="markdown"/>
		</combobox>
		<label value="(the document below stays the same; only the grammar changes)"/>
	</hlayout>
	<codeeditor id="sampler" language="javascript" height="150px" width="600px">
		<attribute name="value">/* the same text under every grammar */
const limit = 25;
function pick(rows) { return rows.filter(r =&gt; r.total &gt; limit); }</attribute>
	</codeeditor>

	<n:h1>lineNumbers and tabSize</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	lineNumbers toggles the gutter (default true). tabSize is the displayed width
	of a tab, 4 by default; the indent character itself is always a tab, so
	tabSize changes how the same file looks, never what it contains. A tabSize
	below 1 raises a WrongValueException.
	</n:p>
	<hlayout valign="middle">
		<label value="no gutter, tabs 8 columns wide"/>
	</hlayout>
	<codeeditor language="xml" lineNumbers="false" tabSize="8" height="120px" width="600px">
		<attribute name="value">&lt;routes&gt;
	&lt;route path="/orders" service="order-api"&gt;
		&lt;timeout ms="2000"/&gt;
	&lt;/route&gt;
&lt;/routes&gt;</attribute>
	</codeeditor>

	<n:h1>Theme</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	theme is light (default) or dark; dark adds the z-codeeditor-dark modifier and
	swaps the surface plus the token palette. Any other non-null value raises a
	WrongValueException.
	</n:p>
	<codeeditor language="css" theme="dark" height="140px" width="600px">
		<attribute name="value">.z-button {
	/* dark surface, VS Code Dark+ token colours */
	border-radius: 4px;
	padding: 6px 14px;
}</attribute>
	</codeeditor>

	<n:h1>readonly and disabled</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	readonly keeps the editor focusable and its text selectable and copyable - the
	right choice for a code viewer. disabled also drops it out of the tab order,
	blocks the pointer and dims it.
	</n:p>
	<codeeditor language="json" readonly="true" height="110px" width="600px">
		<attribute name="value">{
	"readonly": true,
	"note": "click into me, select this line, copy it"
}</attribute>
	</codeeditor>
	<codeeditor language="json" disabled="true" height="110px" width="600px">
		<attribute name="value">{
	"disabled": true,
	"note": "dimmed, not focusable, Tab skips over me"
}</attribute>
	</codeeditor>

	<n:h1>Keyboard</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	Tab moves focus to the next control and Shift+Tab to the previous one, so the
	editor is never a keyboard trap. Indent and outdent inside the document with
	Ctrl+] and Ctrl+[ (Cmd on macOS). Undo and redo are Ctrl/Cmd+Z and
	Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+Z.
	</n:p>
	<hlayout valign="middle">
		<textbox placeholder="Tab from here..."/>
		<label value="into the editor, then Tab again to reach the button"/>
	</hlayout>
	<codeeditor language="sql" height="90px" width="600px" value="SELECT * FROM orders"/>
	<button label="the next stop"/>

	<n:h1>onChange and onChanging</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	both carry an org.zkoss.zk.ui.event.InputEvent. onChanging fires while typing;
	onChange fires when the edit is committed, which for this component means when
	the editor loses focus - so click outside it to see the second counter move.
	</n:p>
	<codeeditor id="watched" language="markdown" height="110px" width="600px"
			onChanging='changingCount.setValue("onChanging: " + (++typing)
					+ " (" + event.getValue().length() + " chars)")'
			onChange='changeCount.setValue("onChange: committed "
					+ event.getValue().length() + " chars")'>
		<attribute name="value"># Release notes

Type here, then click away.</attribute>
	</codeeditor>
	<zscript>int typing = 0;</zscript>
	<vlayout>
		<label id="changingCount" value="onChanging: 0"/>
		<label id="changeCount" value="onChange: not committed yet"/>
	</vlayout>

	<n:h1>Client-side API</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	the widget zul.code.Codeeditor exposes setValue, setLanguage, setReadonly,
	setDisabled, setLineNumbers, setTabSize and setTheme (plus the matching
	getters). Called from the browser they reconfigure the live editor with no
	server round-trip - useful for a toolbar that only changes how code is
	displayed.
	</n:p>
	<hlayout>
		<button label="dark" onClick='clientSide.setTheme("dark")'/>
		<button label="light" onClick='clientSide.setTheme("light")'/>
		<button label="gutter off" onClick='clientSide.setLineNumbers(false)'/>
		<button label="gutter on" onClick='clientSide.setLineNumbers(true)'/>
		<button label="as sql" onClick='clientSide.setLanguage("sql")'/>
		<button label="as plain" onClick='clientSide.setLanguage("plain")'/>
	</hlayout>
	<codeeditor id="clientSide" language="sql" height="120px" width="600px">
		<attribute name="value">SELECT customer_id, SUM(total) AS revenue
FROM orders
WHERE status = 'SHIPPED'
GROUP BY customer_id</attribute>
	</codeeditor>

	<n:h1>Data binding</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	value is two-way bindable and saves on onChange, so @bind(vm.source) writes
	the edited text back when the editor loses focus. Edit the XML below, click
	outside the editor, then press Deploy - the view model parses whatever it
	received.
	</n:p>
	<vlayout viewModel="@id('vm')@init('org.zkoss.reference.component.input.CodeeditorVM')">
		<codeeditor language="xml" height="150px" width="600px" value="@bind(vm.source)"/>
		<hlayout valign="middle">
			<button label="Deploy" onClick="@command('deploy')"/>
			<label value="@load(vm.status)"/>
		</hlayout>
	</vlayout>

	<n:h1>Accessible name</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	there is no label property; give the editor its accessible name through the
	client/attribute namespace and the widget forwards it onto CodeMirror's
	editable region, where a screen reader looks for it. A readonly editor also
	exposes aria-readonly.
	</n:p>
	<codeeditor ca:aria-label="Deployment descriptor editor"
				language="xml" height="100px" width="600px"
				value="&lt;web-app version=&quot;4.0&quot;/&gt;"/>
	<label id="visibleName" value="Startup script"/>
	<codeeditor ca:aria-labelledby="${visibleName.uuid}"
				language="javascript" height="100px" width="600px"
				value="window.addEventListener('load', boot);"/>

	<n:h1>Restyling the dark surface</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	the dark surface and every syntax token read a CSS custom property on the
	.z-codeeditor root, so a theme - or one element's style - can repaint them.
	The surface hooks are --zk-codeeditor-background, -color, -gutter-color and
	-active-line; the token hooks are --zk-codeeditor-token- plus keyword, string,
	comment, number, function, type, variable, tag, attribute or meta.
	</n:p>
	<codeeditor language="javascript" theme="dark" height="140px" width="600px"
			style="--zk-codeeditor-background:#0b1021;
				   --zk-codeeditor-color:#c0caf5;
				   --zk-codeeditor-gutter-color:#3b4261;
				   --zk-codeeditor-token-keyword:#bb9af7;
				   --zk-codeeditor-token-string:#9ece6a;
				   --zk-codeeditor-token-number:#ff9e64;
				   --zk-codeeditor-token-comment:#565f89;">
		<attribute name="value">// the same dark theme, repainted by seven custom properties
const retries = 3;
function boot(cfg) {
	return cfg.enabled ? "started" : "skipped";
}</attribute>
	</codeeditor>

	<n:h1>Use Cases</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	Two screens where a codeeditor is the working surface rather than a sample.
	Only the editor and the values it drives are real; the framing is plain
	markup and CSS.
	</n:p>

	<style>
		.uc-card {
			width: 720px;
			margin-bottom: 12px;
			border: 1px solid #d5dbe1;
			border-radius: 6px;
			background: #fff;
		}
		.uc-card .z-label { font-size: 13px; }
		.uc-crumb {
			padding: 6px 12px;
			border-radius: 5px 5px 0 0;
			background: #2f4a63;
			color: #c9d8e6;
			font-size: 12px;
			letter-spacing: .04em;
		}
		.uc-crumb b { color: #fff; }
		.uc-body { padding: 12px; }
		.uc-note {
			padding: 8px 12px;
			border-top: 1px solid #eef1f4;
			color: #6b7785;
			font-size: 12px;
		}
		.uc-ok { color: #1a7f37; font-weight: bold; }
		.uc-bad { color: #b3261e; font-weight: bold; }
		.uc-preview {
			padding: 10px;
			border: 1px dashed #c7ced6;
			border-radius: 4px;
			background: #fbfcfd;
		}
	</style>

	<n:h2>Marketing: an email template editor with preview</n:h2>
	<vlayout sclass="uc-card" spacing="0">
		<div sclass="uc-crumb">
			<label value="Campaigns / Autumn Sale / "/><label value="Template" sclass="uc-crumb"/>
		</div>
		<vlayout sclass="uc-body">
			<codeeditor id="tpl" language="html" height="180px" hflex="1">
				<attribute name="value">&lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif"&gt;
	&lt;h2 style="color:#b3261e"&gt;Autumn Sale&lt;/h2&gt;
	&lt;p&gt;Hello ${'$'}{firstName}, everything in the outlet is &lt;b&gt;30% off&lt;/b&gt;
	   until Sunday.&lt;/p&gt;
	&lt;a href="#" style="color:#2f4a63"&gt;Browse the outlet&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</attribute>
			</codeeditor>
			<hlayout valign="middle">
				<button label="Preview" onClick="renderTemplate()"/>
				<label id="tplStatus" value="not rendered yet"/>
			</hlayout>
			<div id="tplPreview" sclass="uc-preview"/>
		</vlayout>
		<div sclass="uc-note">
			<label value="Preview reads tpl.getValue() on the server, so the editor's current text is whatever the marketer last committed - click outside the editor before pressing Preview."/>
		</div>
	</vlayout>

	<zscript><![CDATA[
		void renderTemplate() {
			String source = tpl.getValue();
			tplPreview.getChildren().clear();
			Html preview = new Html();
			preview.setContent(source.replace("${firstName}", "Dana"));
			tplPreview.appendChild(preview);
			tplStatus.setValue("rendered " + source.length() + " chars");
			tplStatus.setSclass("uc-ok");
		}
	]]></zscript>

	<n:h2>Operations: a read-only config snapshot viewer</n:h2>
	<vlayout sclass="uc-card" spacing="0">
		<div sclass="uc-crumb">
			<label value="Operations / gateway-prod / "/><label value="Snapshots" sclass="uc-crumb"/>
		</div>
		<hlayout sclass="uc-body" valign="top">
			<listbox id="snapshots" width="230px" height="200px"
					 onSelect="showSnapshot(self.getSelectedItem().getValue())">
				<listhead>
					<listheader label="Deployed"/>
				</listhead>
			</listbox>
			<vlayout hflex="1">
				<codeeditor id="snapshotView" language="json" readonly="true"
							theme="dark" height="200px" hflex="1"/>
				<label id="snapshotNote"/>
			</vlayout>
		</hlayout>
		<div sclass="uc-note">
			<label value="readonly rather than disabled: an operator still needs to select and copy a line out of an old snapshot."/>
		</div>
	</vlayout>

	<zscript><![CDATA[
		java.util.Map SNAPSHOTS = new java.util.LinkedHashMap();
		SNAPSHOTS.put("2026-08-31 14:02  rollout", "{\n" +
				"  \"upstream\": \"order-api-v3\",\n" +
				"  \"timeoutMs\": 2000,\n" +
				"  \"retries\": 2,\n" +
				"  \"circuitBreaker\": { \"enabled\": true, \"failureRatio\": 0.5 }\n" +
				"}");
		SNAPSHOTS.put("2026-08-24 09:41  hotfix", "{\n" +
				"  \"upstream\": \"order-api-v2\",\n" +
				"  \"timeoutMs\": 8000,\n" +
				"  \"retries\": 0,\n" +
				"  \"circuitBreaker\": { \"enabled\": false }\n" +
				"}");
		SNAPSHOTS.put("2026-08-11 17:20  baseline", "{\n" +
				"  \"upstream\": \"order-api-v2\",\n" +
				"  \"timeoutMs\": 5000,\n" +
				"  \"retries\": 1,\n" +
				"  \"circuitBreaker\": { \"enabled\": true, \"failureRatio\": 0.8 }\n" +
				"}");

		void showSnapshot(String when) {
			String json = (String) SNAPSHOTS.get(when);
			snapshotView.setValue(json);
			snapshotNote.setValue(when + "  -  " + json.split("\n").length + " lines, read-only");
		}

		for (java.util.Iterator it = SNAPSHOTS.keySet().iterator(); it.hasNext();) {
			String when = (String) it.next();
			Listitem item = new Listitem(when);
			item.setValue(when);
			snapshots.appendChild(item);
		}
		/* open on the newest snapshot rather than on an empty editor */
		snapshots.setSelectedIndex(0);
		showSnapshot((String) snapshots.getSelectedItem().getValue());
	]]></zscript>
</zk>
